                   AltaVista Announces Windows NT
                       Intranet Pack Promotion


 ...Limited-time Special Offer on Mail, Directory and Forum Trio to 
                   Power Up Corporate Intranets...


MAYNARD, Mass., March 10, 1997 - AltaVista Internet Software, Inc., 
a subsidiary of Digital Equipment Corporation, today announced the
AltaVista NT Intranet Pack, a bundle of three easy-to-use and 
install intranet information and messaging tools for Windows NT.  
The AltaVista NT Intranet Pack includes AltaVista Mail Server 97, 
AltaVista Directory 97 and AltaVista Forum.  Until June 30, 1997, 
the package is available worldwide for a special promotional price 
of $995 (USD), a savings of $490.  The pack is available through 
resellers and distributors; a complete list can be accessed on the 
Web at  http://altavista.software.digital.com.

     "The AltaVista NT Intranet Pack offers business a fast, 
cost-effective way to provide critical information to employees 
globally," said Ilene H. Lang, president and CEO of AltaVista 
Internet Software, Inc. and vice president of Digital. "It's another 
demonstration of our 'OnSite Computing' strategy, leveraging the 
power of the Internet and intranets to let users conduct business 
from anywhere."

     Featuring built-in connectivity to the Internet, AltaVista Mail 
provides departments and small enterprises with powerful, low-cost 
Internet mail capabilities that can be added to a web server or 
existing electronic mail software - including the ability to mail 
multimedia documents over the Internet.  AltaVista Mail Server 97, 
which includes a 250-user license, integrates seamlessly with 
enterprise mail systems such as Microsoft Exchange. AltaVista Mail 
Internet eXtensions are also available as options for cc:Mail and 
Microsoft Mail.

     AltaVista Directory 97 is an intelligent and powerful 
out-of-the-box personnel directory application.  Directory 97 
includes innovative phonetic search capabilities and is 
client-independent.  Users can access it with their favorite Web 
browser from any platform, and can also access it from any e-mail 
client that supports LDAP (Lightweight Directory Access Protocol), 
MAPI, ph and Finger e-mail applications. AltaVista Directory 97 
includes a 250-user license and provides state-of-the-art management 
capabilities, making it much faster and easier to network, 
configure, and update corporate directories while supporting 
hundreds of thousands of entries.

     AltaVista Forum is the perfect complement for users with 
Microsoft Office, providing a Web-accessible library for Office 
documents.  In addition, AltaVista Forum conferencing capabilities 
let business teams and workgroups hold secure, "virtual" meetings 
over the Internet from anywhere at any time from any desktop 
platform with a World Wide Web browser.  AltaVista Forum with a 
25-user license is included in the AltaVista NT Productivity Pack. 

     AltaVista OnSite Computing Solutions provide secure, simple, 
and direct access to information and people over the Internet and 
private intranets. AltaVista Search, Directory, Tunnel, Firewall, 
Forum, and Mail products give users a competitive edge, enabling 
productive business to take place from anywhere. Further information 
on the AltaVista NT Intranet Pack promotion and AltaVista OnSite 
Computing is available at http://altavista.software.digital.com 
or by calling 1-800-336-7890.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software, and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.

