             DIGITAL, MetaWare Announce Embedded Toolset
                Optimizations for StrongARM Processor


              ...Feature-Specific Enhancements Increase
                     Application Performance...


MAYNARD, Mass., March 10, 1997 -- Digital Equipment Corporation and 
MetaWare Incorporated today announced that MetaWare will optimize 
its High C/C++ Embedded Software Development Toolset specifically 
for the StrongARM microprocessor from Digital Semiconductor, a 
Digital Equipment Corporation business.  The StrongARM optimizations 
will be available this summer.

     In a related announcement, MetaWare today introduced a version 
of the High C/C++ Embedded Development Toolset for the ARM 
architecture.

     MetaWare's flagship product, the High C/C++ compiler, combines 
a proven C/C++ compiler front end with platform-specific, code-
generator back ends.  The High C/C++ Embedded Development Toolset 
for the ARM architecture contains quality enhancement features such 
as branch prediction for improved code generation, staged migration 
of projects from C to C++, a branch profile lister that alerts 
developers to code "hot spots," and improved interrupt handler and 
runtime information access functions.

Optimized for StrongARM Features

     The High C/C++ toolset optimizations will take advantage of 
specific StrongARM features and functional differences from other 
ARM processors to generate the most efficient and compact code for 
StrongARM embedded applications.  They include support for StrongARM 
processor-specific instructions; code and data alignment to take 
advantage of the StrongARM dual-cache structure; scheduling 
optimization for the SA-110 five-stage pipeline; and improved branch 
optimization.

     Digital Semiconductor estimates that C and C++ programs for 
StrongARM developed with these processor-specific features should 
see a performance boost of approximately 10 percent over non-
optimized programs.  Improvements of approximately 20 percent are 
estimated for multiply-intensive programs such as digital signal 
processor (DSP)- oriented applications.

Powerful Tools for Customers

     Gili Keshet-Aspitz, Digital Semiconductor's marketing manager 
for StrongARM development tools, said, "As our line of StrongARM 
processors becomes increasingly popular in the market, our goal is 
to have the most effective and powerful development tools available 
to help our customers produce compact, fast StrongARM programs for 
real-world deployment.  With the high quality and exceptional 
performance offered by the High C/C++ product set, MetaWare is 
helping us meet that goal."

     "MetaWare is delighted to be able to offer the highest-quality 
C and C++ tools for  software developers targeting the StrongARM 
microprocessor," said John Ryal, chief operating officer of MetaWare 
Incorporated.  "The many professional features of MetaWare's High C/C++ 
ARM Embedded Software Development Toolset will help speed cost-effective 
StrongARM- based designs to production with software that uses the 
unique characteristics of this processor.  MetaWare's performance-
oriented tools are a perfect complement to the StrongARM processor, 
making it a leader in the fast-growing, performance-critical markets 
targeted by Digital."

     Digital Semiconductor, a Digital Equipment Corporation business 
headquartered in Hudson, Massachusetts, designs, manufactures and 
markets industry-leading semiconductor products including Alpha 
microprocessors and PCI chips for networking, bridging, and 
multimedia, plus low-power StrongARM microprocessors under license 
from Advanced RISC Machines Ltd.  Mitsubishi Electric Corporation 
and Samsung Electronics Company Ltd. are alternate sources for Alpha 
microprocessors.  Web site:  http://www.digital.com/semiconductor

