            DIGITAL Expands Storage Management Solutions
                         for the Enterprise


MAYNARD, Mass., March 24, 1997 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced a broad range of storage management tools for the 
enterprise that allow customers to backup and archive mission-
critical data created with the industry's leading applications. The 
company also announced hierarchical storage management (HSM) 
software to better manage disk space.

     "Managing the explosive growth of data in an enterprise, which 
now extends well into the terabyte range, is one of the greatest 
challenges our customers face," said Dave Coombs, vice president of 
Storage Marketing at Digital.  "It's no longer possible for them to 
schedule data transfers, backups, and archives during periods of 
downtime. Today's announcement strengthens Digital's portfolio of 
enterprise storage management solutions with new products that 
automatically protect data from mission-critical databases and 
applications. Customers are now able to store, share, back up, and 
archive online data in mixed client/server environments." 

Enterprise Modules for NetWorker Save and Restore 

     Part of today's announcement includes new modules for Digital's
NetWorker Save and Restore software, which provides automated 
backup, recovery, and archiving of data in a networked environment. 
The new modules help administrators ensure that data from business-
critical database applications is protected and available 24 hours a 
day, seven days a week. They are, as follows: 

     o 	NetWorker Save and Restore Module for Microsoft Exchange and 
        NetWorker Save and Restore Module for SQL Server, which 
        allow customers to perform online back up and restore from 
        Microsoft Exchange and Microsoft SQL Server databases. 

     o 	NetWorker Save and Restore Application Interface for SAP R3, 
        an integrated solution for backing up large volumes of SAP 
        R3 data. It offers simplified administration, powerful media 
        management, and unsurpassed performance.

     o 	NetWorker HSM Module for Digital UNIX, which allows 
        customers to manage disk space by migrating less frequently 
        used files to near- or off-line storage. With less online 
        storage, backups are less costly and time consuming. 


Windows NT Support for Archive/Backup System Software

     A new version of Digital's Archive/Backup System software 
enables customers with OpenVMS servers to archive or back up data 
from Windows NT clients. The product, which protects enterprise 
applications with automated backup, restore, and archiving 
capabilities, lowers the chances of accidental file loss. The 
software, which also supports six UNIX platforms, is ideal for 
enterprise customers with multivendor, networked environments.

New Clients for Digital's InfoServer 1000 

     Digital is also enhancing its InfoServer 1000, a modular 
product that offers virtual storage services for CDs, CD-Recordable, 
disks, and other devices. The InfoServer 1000 now enables Windows NT 
and Digital UNIX clients to share CD-ROMs as part of a local area 
network. Customers can use the system to distribute software and 
data from expensive databases across departments. 

Pricing and Availability

     NetWorker server licenses, required for NetWorker modules, 
start at $2,500 for a Digital UNIX server. The NetWorker HSM Module 
starts at $10,500. The NetWorker Module for Microsoft SQL Server is 
$995. The NetWorker Module for Microsoft Exchange is $995. The 
NetWorker Module for SAP R3 starts at $6,000. The Archive/Backup 
System starts at $2,495; client licenses start at $1,980. The 
InfoServer Client for Digital UNIX and Windows NT are $99 each. 

     The NetWorker Module for SAP R3, Archive/Backup System, and 
InfoServer Client for Windows NT are available now. The InfoServer 
Client for Digital UNIX, NetWorker Module for Exchange, NetWorker 
Module for SQL Server, and the NetWorker HSM Module will be 
available in April.						    

     For more information about Digital's complete line of storage 
hardware and software products, call 1-800-STORWORK (1-800-786-7967) 
or visit http://www.storage.digital.com on the World Wide Web. 

