           Digital Enhances Internet AlphaServer Software
                          for Digital UNIX


           Robust, Fully Integrated Packages Available for
                     Beginners and Veteran Users



MAYNARD, Mass., March 5, 1997 - Digital Equipment Corporation today
announced the release of two robust and fully integrated Internet
software packages for DIGITAL UNIX.  The high-end offering, Internet
AlphaServer Software (IAS) V3.2, is packaged for experienced users 
who need enhanced productivity.  The second package, Internet 
AlphaServer Systems Software (IASS) V3.2 accommodates the less 
demanding needs of the entry-level user.  This script-driven, fully 
integrated Internet software is easy to install, administer and use. 

     "Continuing to respond to our customers requests for added 
Internet solutions, we are pleased to offer improved Internet 
AlphaServer software for DIGITAL UNIX," said Rose Ann Giordano, vice 
president of Digital's Internet Business Group.  "In addition to 
added functionality, users of our two new DIGITAL UNIX software 
packages gain the superior speed and performance of 64-bit Alpha 
computing."

New features in this product release include:


     * 	Squid Proxy/Caching Server enhances performance by caching 
        frequently used information so that it can be accessed 
        quickly; responds up to 4 times faster than other commonly 
        used proxy/caching products.

     * 	Internet Relay Chat (IRC) client and server support allows 
        users to communicate (chat) with others in real-time.

     * 	Domain Name Server (DNS) provides failover functionality 
        that gives the user the security of no downtime; if one 
        system node fails, the system will remain active by 
        switching (failing over) to another node.

     * 	Updated Public Software to the most recent releases lets the 
        user stay up-to-date with security enhancements, increased 
        performance and/or functionality improvements made to the 
        chosen software products in IAS and IASS.


     The high-end package, IAS for DIGITAL UNIX, ships as a 
stand-alone package, with Internet AlphaServer ENERGIZED PLUS 
systems, and TruCluster Available Servers. DIGITAL announced 
Internet ENERGIZED PLUS systems in December 1996.  These systems 
offer a suite of Internet products, including IAS, POLYCENTER 
NetView, and PATROL Knowledge Module.  As a result, DIGITAL UNIX 
Internet AlphaServer systems are not only Internet-ready, but also 
Internet-robust.

Internet AlphaServer Software for DIGITAL UNIX

     IAS includes: Netscape Enterprise Server for HTTP document
creation/publication and secure electronic commerce transactions on 
the Internet; Internet Administration Software for HTML-based user, 
printer, and configuration management; carefully selected public 
software such as Apache Web Server, Perl, Bind, Squid, sendmail, 
IMAP, POP-3, INN News Server, Major Domo List Server, Washington 
University-FTP, Internet Relay Chat (IRC) TCPwrapper; trial software 
for Enhanced CU-SeeMe and Reflector from White Pine; the DIGITAL 
UNIX Operating System CD-ROM; and hardcopy documentation.

Internet AlphaServer Systems Software for DIGITAL UNIX

     The entry level offering, IASS for DIGITAL UNIX, ships as a 
stand alone package and with all DIGITAL UNIX AlphaServers.  IASS 
includes all of the components of IAS except Netscape Enterprise 
Server and the hardcopy documentation.

     "Users of both IAS and IASS gain the benefits of the 
unprecedented speed and performance of 64-bit Alpha computing on 
DIGITAL UNIX systems. This is especially important in the Internet 
Service Provider (ISP) marketplace," said Digital's ISP marketing 
manager Mark Conway.  "ISPs are some of our most demanding 
customers. The enhancements announced today provide them with the 
platforms and performance they need to offer reliable, value-added 
services.  These packages make any standalone AlphaServer an 
immediate and outstanding mail, web, news or DNS server - right out 
of the box."

Pricing and Availability

     Both packages will be available from DIGITAL and its resellers 
on March 14, 1997.  Internet AlphaServer Software V3.2 for DIGITAL 
UNIX is priced at $1295 worldwide.  Internet AlphaServer Systems 
Software V3.2 for DIGITAL UNIX is priced at $495 worldwide. Call 
1-800-DIGITAL for ordering information.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems.  DIGITAL's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.

