           Digital Announces Packaged Integration Services
   to Support Microsoft's Commercial Internet System Product Suite


MAYNARD, Mass., March 6, 1997 - Digital Equipment Corporation 
announced today the availability of packaged integration services 
specific to Microsoft's new Commercial Internet System (MCIS) 
product suite for Windows NT.  DIGITAL's Internet services and 
solutions support the rapid implementation of MCIS, and lay the 
groundwork for addressing the intricacies of Web publishing and site 
management, as well as setting up communications and collaboration 
tools.  

     MCIS, whose project code was Normandy, is a comprehensive set 
of Internet server software applications for Internet Service 
Providers, network operators, and Internet content providers.  This 
integrated set of applications can be configured to support the 
client's vision for conducting business online.  MCIS is also used 
to cultivate "communities of interest" whose members use interactive 
tools to collaborate and communicate.  Under the terms of an 
existing agreement with Microsoft, DIGITAL is a premier integrator 
of MCIS.  

     With today's announcement, DIGITAL offers two choices to speed 
entry into the Internet service business - MCIS Planning and MCIS 
Pilot Service.

     *	MCIS Planning is designed to help providers understand the
     	capabilities of the Microsoft Commercial Internet Systems 
        applications, and find additional products to complete their 
        Internet offerings.
 
     *	MCIS Pilot Service is for those providers who are ready to 
        test new service offerings for their customers. 


Related offerings from DIGITAL Services are targeted to public 
network operators.  


     *	Integration Services for MCIS help develop, configure, and 
        install business applications such as billing, trouble 
        ticket, ad insertion, merchant, and order fulfillment. The 
        service also includes the integration of MCIS with legacy 
        applications such as enterprise resource planning, financial 
        and business applications, and customer service tools.
 
     *	Infrastructure Services are offered to plan, design, and 
        implement the required network infrastructure and/or the 
        data center for the smooth operation of the MCIS system.
  
     *	Security Services, such as firewalls, encryption, and 
        tunnels, secure the client's environment against breaches 
        and protect the network, sensitive data, and applications.
 
     *	Operations Management Services are available to outsource 
        the day-to-day running of the network, data center, help 
        desk, and the facilities.


     "DIGITAL has helped more than 100 Internet Service Providers 
around the world to establish their business for the Internet," said 
Rick Mace, vice president of DIGITAL's Internet Services business.  
"We are now coupling this knowledge with our unequaled NT and 
networks expertise and a strong suite of products from Microsoft  to 
enable network operators to go online."

     According to Cameron Myhrvold, vice president, Microsoft, 
"DIGITAL has professionals trained on MCIS than any other integrator 
in the world.  In addition, DIGITAL has a greater number of 
completed or in-process MCIS engagements, including projects at 
Telecom Eireann, Singapore Cablevision, Camby Cable, and 
Post-Newsweek."

